Q4. Locator Selection

 1. Preferred Locator

I would choose the **ID locator: `btn-confirm-order`**.

Reason:

- ID locators are generally unique and reliable.
- The button ID remains stable even when the DOM structure changes.
- XPath depends on the button's position inside the parent div.
- If the DOM structure changes, the XPath may fail or locate the wrong element.

2. Definition of Fragile Locator

A fragile locator is a locator that can easily break when the HTML or DOM structure of a web page changes.

Example

`//div[@class='checkout-wrapper']/button[3]`

This XPath depends on the button's position. If another button is added or the order of buttons changes, the locator may stop working.

3. Consequence in Regression Testing

Using fragile locators in every sprint can cause automated test cases to fail even when the actual application functionality is working correctly. This creates unnecessary test maintenance and false failures.
